
Jutze Japan Motion Coordinate Board ver. 1.3 (PBJP1702A)

The board has been specifically designed for various pick-and-place board
options.  This means that the same PCB can be used to get different board
variants with different amount of functionality.  It is possible to use
different RX MCU versions and also omit or include most of the functional
blocks.

The following macros are available to control some BSP options during
compile time:

MCB_USE_RX631_144
  use the RX631 144pin MCU.

MCB_USE_RX63N_144
  use the RX63N 144pin MCU.

MCB_USE_RX64M_144
  use the RX64M 144pin MCU.

MCB_USE_RX64M_176
  use the RX64M 176pin MCU.

MCB_USE_RX71M_144
  use the RX71M 144pin MCU.

MCB_USE_RX71M_176
  use the RX71M 176pin MCU.


the board variant can also be specified when setting up a build directory:
cmake -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=~/code/MCBcode/toolchain/rx/toolchain.cmake \
      -DCMAKE_BOARD_DIR=~/code/MCBcode/board/mcb_v1.3 \
      -DCMAKE_LIBRARIES_DIR=~/code/MCBcode
      -DBOARD_VARIANT=RX71M_176 \
       ~/code/MCBcode/app/mcb13_test

MCB_USE_I2C
  enable on-board I2C bus on SCI2.

MCB_USE_SPI
  enable on-board write-only SPI bus on SCI4 for DAC control.

MCB_USE_DAC124S085
  enable the DAC124S085 device.

MCB_USE_RS485
  enable the RS485 ports on SCI6 and SCI7 (144pin) / SCIF10 (176pin).

MCB_USE_PCA9698
  enable the on-board PCA9698 bus expanders.

MCB_USE_PCD4641
  enable the PCD4641 device.

MCB_USE_MCX514
  enable the MCX514 device.

MCB_USE_USB_FUNCTION
  enable USB0 function port (144pin and 176pin).

MCB_USE_USB_HOST
  enable USBA host port (176pin only).

MCB_USE_TRIGGER_IO
  enable the board specific trigger_io device.

MCB_USE_LEDS
  enable the board specific led_outputs device.

MCB_USE_DIPSWITCH
  enable the board specific dipswitch_inputs device.

MCB_USE_DIGITAL_IO
  enable the board specific digital_io device.

MCB_USE_RX_ETHERC0
  enable the RX EtherC 0 device (144pin and 176pin, ETH0) as a normal eth device

MCB_USE_RX_ETHERC0_RAW
  enable the RX EtherC 0 device (144pin and 176pin, ETH0) as a raw device

MCB_USE_RX_ETHERC1
  enable the RX EtherC 1 device (176pin, ETH1) as a normal eth device

MCB_USE_RX_ETHERC1_RAW
  enable the RX EtherC 1 device (176pin, ETH1) as a raw device

MCB_USE_LAN9250
  enable the LAN9250 device (ETH2) as a normal eth device

MCB_USE_LAN9250_RAW
  enable the LAN9250 device (ETH2) as a raw device


MCB_USE_FCU
  define to enable the FCU.
  the drivers for RX63 and RX64/RX71 are different.  depending on the selected
  MCU, the appropritate FCU drivers will be used.

MCB_USE_SCI_DEBUG
  define to redirect debugging printf on stdout and stderr to the
  SCI debugging port.

MCB_NO_CRC
  define to disable the RX hardware CRC accelerator device usage.
  normally, it is enabled, depending on the MCU type being used.

MCB_USE_SCI0_UART
MCB_USE_SCI3_UART
MCB_USE_SCI5_UART

